**Advantages**:
- It signals to anyone reading your code that this function is pure and does not depend on object state.
- Python does not pass the instance pointer to it, slightly saving execution overhead.
- It can be called either from an instance (`self.is_valid_char(ch)`) or directly from the class (`Trie.is_valid_char(ch)`).

